From 9cfc5cdb488add4868fd899409c7cbba89a003c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiping Ma <yipingma@berkeley.edu>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:59:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [chore] adapt to non-negative bound goal of pHL rnd
 (EasyCrypt#1135)

EasyCrypt#1135 makes the pHL `rnd` tactic (upper-bound form) emit an extra
last goal `forall &hr, 0%r <= bd`, closed automatically only when trivial.
In the two `gen_bad` lemmas of PKEY.ec the bound `card (fdom (filter ...))%r
* pr_guess` is not, so after `rnd ...; auto` that goal is now discharged with
`smt(ge0_pr_guess fcard_ge0)` before the last `seq` branch is closed by `hoare`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 PKEY.ec | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/PKEY.ec b/PKEY.ec
index 41293d7..343e8e0 100644
--- a/PKEY.ec
+++ b/PKEY.ec
@@ -363,6 +363,7 @@ seq 2: (PKEYb.skm.[pk] = Some Corrupt)
     by move=> pk _; rewrite dmap1E dkp_max.
   move=> [] pk sk /= _.
   by rewrite mem_fdom domE filterE=> ->.
+  by move=> &hr; smt(ge0_pr_guess fcard_ge0).
 by hoare; auto=> />.
 qed.
 
@@ -786,6 +787,7 @@ seq 2: (is_honest PKEYb.skm.[pk])
     by move=> pk _; rewrite dmap1E dkp_max.
   move=> [] pk sk /= _.
   by rewrite mem_fdom domE filterE /is_honest; case: skm.[pk]=> [|[]] /#.
+  by move=> &hr; smt(ge0_pr_guess fcard_ge0).
 by hoare; auto=> /#.
 qed.
 
